<img width="350" height="525" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/Mediterranean-Pasta-Salad-350x525.jpg" class="webfeedsFeaturedVisual wp-post-image" alt="Mediterranean pasta salad in a bowl from the top view." style="display: block; margin-bottom: 5px; clear:both;max-width: 100%;" link_thumbnail="" decoding="async" srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/Mediterranean-Pasta-Salad-350x525.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/Mediterranean-Pasta-Salad-768x1152.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/Mediterranean-Pasta-Salad-1024x1536.jpg 1024w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/Mediterranean-Pasta-Salad-400x600.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/Mediterranean-Pasta-Salad-150x225.jpg 150w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/Mediterranean-Pasta-Salad-735x1103.jpg 735w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/Mediterranean-Pasta-Salad.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 350px) 100vw, 350px" />
<div class="wp-block-group is-layout-constrained wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained">
<p>Even as someone who develops recipes for a living, I still have those moments before a get-together when I&rsquo;m standing in the kitchen wondering, <em>what should I bring?</em> I mean, I know I have a blog full of recipes, but when you&rsquo;re serving a crowd with so many preferences and diet restrictions, it&rsquo;s always a hard decision to make.</p>



<p>My experience is that this Mediterranean macaroni salad seems to please most people. For one thing, most people love the familiar &ldquo;Greek&rdquo; flavors (i.e. cucumbers, olives, tomatoes, etc.) and it rarely needs an introduction. To me, it is like a bistro pasta salad that is the most popular dish on the menu.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image aligncenter size-full"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="1800" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/Bowtie-pasta-salad-Mediterranean.jpg" alt="Cold Mediterranean pasta salad in a bowl with wooden spoons from the top view." class="wp-image-81561" srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/Bowtie-pasta-salad-Mediterranean.jpg 1200w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/Bowtie-pasta-salad-Mediterranean-350x525.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/Bowtie-pasta-salad-Mediterranean-768x1152.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/Bowtie-pasta-salad-Mediterranean-1024x1536.jpg 1024w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/Bowtie-pasta-salad-Mediterranean-400x600.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/Bowtie-pasta-salad-Mediterranean-150x225.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/Bowtie-pasta-salad-Mediterranean.jpg"></figure>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-key-ingredients">Key Ingredients:</h2>



<p>The good news is that once you understand the process and the flavor profile, it&rsquo;s easy to make this Mediterranean pasta recipe your own. You can find the full list of ingredients in the recipe card below, but below are a few helpful notes and substitutions:</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image aligncenter size-large"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="800" data-pin-nopin="true" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/Ingredients-for-pasta-salad-Mediterranean-1200x800.jpg" alt="Ingredients for the recipe from the top view with text on the image." class="wp-image-81595" srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/Ingredients-for-pasta-salad-Mediterranean.jpg 1200w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/Ingredients-for-pasta-salad-Mediterranean-350x233.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/Ingredients-for-pasta-salad-Mediterranean-768x512.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/Ingredients-for-pasta-salad-Mediterranean-400x267.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/Ingredients-for-pasta-salad-Mediterranean-150x100.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/Ingredients-for-pasta-salad-Mediterranean.jpg"></figure>



<p><strong>Pasta:</strong> I used farfalle (also known as bow tie pasta), but other shapes like rotini and fusilli would also work. I prefer these shapes as they hold on to the dressing, blend well with the rest of the ingredients, and are easy to scoop and eat cold. Of course, you can always use gluten-free pasta if preferred.&nbsp;</p>



<p><strong>Canned &amp; fresh veggies</strong>: In my humble opinion, using a combination of canned and fresh vegetables is what makes this Mediterranean noodle salad a winner. And the best part is that if you do not have one ingredient (or you don&rsquo;t care for it), you can use another. Here are a few optional add-ins and substitution ideas:</p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong>Onion:</strong> Use finely chopped red onion instead of scallions.</li>



<li><strong>Tomatoes:</strong> If tomatoes are not in season, use finely chopped sun-dried tomatoes instead.</li>



<li><strong>Fresh Herbs: </strong>Fresh oregano is the classic &ldquo;Mediterranean&rdquo; herb used in salads like this, but other herbs like fresh parsley, dill, and mint would all work.</li>



<li><strong>Cheese:</strong> Not a fan of feta cheese? Use goat or no cheese if you prefer a vegan or dairy-free version of this pasta salad.&nbsp;</li>



<li><strong>Add protein: </strong>If you want to turn this into a more filling meal, feel free to bulk it up with a protein. Chickpeas are a great plant-based option and work beautifully with the Mediterranean flavors. You can also add <a href="https://foolproofliving.com/grilled-shrimp-skewers/">grilled shrimp</a>, chicken, or even canned tuna for a quick boost. Just be sure everything is cooled before mixing it in.</li>



<li><strong>Pasta Salad Dressing:</strong> I used my go-to <a href="https://foolproofliving.com/mediterranean-salad-dressing/">Mediterranean Vinaigrette</a>, but my <a href="https://foolproofliving.com/lemon-balsamic-dressing/">Lemon Balsamic Vinaigrette</a> would also be a great dressing option.</li>
</ul>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-how-to-make-mediterranean-pasta-salad">How to Make Mediterranean Pasta Salad?</h2>



<p>Once you have the ingredients ready, making this <strong>Mediterranean diet pasta salad</strong> is no more than a few easy steps. You can find the detailed recipe below, but here&rsquo;s how I put it together:</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="744" data-pin-nopin="true" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/cold-pasta-salad-Mediterranean.jpg" alt="A collage of images showing cooked pasta and making of the pasta salad dressing." class="wp-image-81578" srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/cold-pasta-salad-Mediterranean.jpg 1200w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/cold-pasta-salad-Mediterranean-350x217.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/cold-pasta-salad-Mediterranean-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/cold-pasta-salad-Mediterranean-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/cold-pasta-salad-Mediterranean-150x93.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/cold-pasta-salad-Mediterranean.jpg"></figure>



<p><strong>Step 1 &ndash; Cook the pasta:</strong> I feel like most pasta salads either have too much pasta or too many &ldquo;supporting&rdquo; ingredients. For a salad with so many add-ins, I find that 8 ounces of pasta (which gives you about 4 cups cooked) is the right balance.</p>



<p>Cook it in well-salted boiling water until al dente, according to the package instructions. Then drain and rinse under cold water to stop the cooking process.</p>


<div class="su-note" style="border-color:#d9d8d7;border-radius:1px;-moz-border-radius:1px;-webkit-border-radius:1px;"><div class="su-note-inner su-u-clearfix su-u-trim" style="background-color:#f3f2f1;border-color:#ffffff;color:#000;border-radius:1px;-moz-border-radius:1px;-webkit-border-radius:1px;">



<p><strong>Pro tip:</strong> Let the pasta cool completely before adding the rest of the ingredients. If it&rsquo;s too warm, it can wilt the veggies or melt the cheese. Plus, the dressing will soak in too quickly, leaving the salad a bit dry.</p>


</div></div>



<p><strong>Step 2: Make the dressing: </strong>You can make the Mediterranean pasta salad dressing in a mason jar (great if you&rsquo;re making it ahead) or a measuring cup, but if I&rsquo;m making this for just us at home, I usually grab a large bowl and make it right there.&nbsp;</p>



<p>That way, (1) I don&rsquo;t have to wash another dish, and (2) I can start building the salad directly in the bowl.</p>



<p>No matter what vessel you&rsquo;re using, start by adding the lemon juice, garlic, Dijon mustard, oregano, salt, and pepper. Then, slowly drizzle in the olive oil while whisking. This helps emulsify the dressing, making it a little creamy and helping it cling to the pasta.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image aligncenter size-full"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="744" data-pin-nopin="true" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/pasta-salad-Mediterranean.jpg" alt="Photos showing how to assemble the Mediterranean noodle salad." class="wp-image-81579" srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/pasta-salad-Mediterranean.jpg 1200w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/pasta-salad-Mediterranean-350x217.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/pasta-salad-Mediterranean-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/pasta-salad-Mediterranean-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/pasta-salad-Mediterranean-150x93.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/pasta-salad-Mediterranean.jpg"></figure>



<p><strong>Step 3 &ndash; Assemble the salad:</strong> Grab a large salad bowl. And I do mean large because we&rsquo;ve got a good amount of vegetables going in. Add the cooled pasta along with the rest of the ingredients. It&rsquo;ll look like a pile at first, and that&rsquo;s totally fine.</p>



<p><strong>Step 4: Dress and serve:</strong> Drizzle with the dressing and toss to combine. It might get a little messy, but that&rsquo;s part of the charm of this easy pasta salad. Use tongs or two large spoons, and be gentle (and patient) as you toss.</p>



<p>If you have the time, cover and let it sit in the fridge for 30 minutes so the flavors can mingle.</p>
</div>



<div class="wp-block-group is-layout-constrained wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained"><div class="su-note" style="border-color:#d9d8d7;border-radius:1px;-moz-border-radius:1px;-webkit-border-radius:1px;"><div class="su-note-inner su-u-clearfix su-u-trim" style="background-color:#f3f2f1;border-color:#ffffff;color:#000;border-radius:1px;-moz-border-radius:1px;-webkit-border-radius:1px;">



<h2 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-expert-tips">Expert Tips:</h2>



<p>Before you start cooking, here are a few tips to help you get the best results from this cold Mediterranean pasta salad. These small details can make a big difference in taste, texture, and presentation.</p>



<p><strong>Drain the canned vegetables:</strong> One of the reasons this salad is so convenient is that it takes advantage of canned or jarred ingredients like artichoke hearts, roasted bell peppers, and olives. But if you don&rsquo;t drain them properly, they can add too much moisture and water down the salad. Use a colander and drain each ingredient thoroughly before adding it to the bowl.</p>



<p><strong>Taste for seasoning:</strong> Whenever I write a recipe with salty or briny ingredients like feta cheese and olives, I keep the added salt to a minimum. But let&rsquo;s face it, not all feta or olives are created equal. Some are much saltier than others. So it&rsquo;s always a good idea to taste those components first, then adjust the amount of salt in the dressing as needed.</p>



<p><strong>Chop everything into similar sizes: </strong>For the best texture and an even bite, keep all the ingredients around the same size as the pasta. It&rsquo;s a small thing, but it helps everything mix well and makes the salad easier to eat.</p>


</div></div>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-serving-suggestions">Serving Suggestions:</h2>



<p>While this Mediterranean bow tie pasta salad can stand on its own, it also pairs well with a variety of main dishes. Below are a few of my favorite ways to serve it:</p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong>Roasted or grilled meat and seafood:</strong> This pasta salad is the ideal companion to a simply <a href="https://foolproofliving.com/grilled-sockeye-salmon/">grilled salmon</a>,&nbsp; <a href="https://foolproofliving.com/baked-bone-in-chicken-breast/">baked chicken breast</a>, or even lamb chops. The fresh, vibrant flavors of the salad beautifully cut through the richness of grilled proteins, making for a light yet satisfying meal.</li>



<li><strong>Make it a Mediterranean weeknight dinner:</strong> Make a batch of my mom&rsquo;s <a href="https://foolproofliving.com/chicken-kofta/">Chicken Kofta Recipe</a> and serve it with your pasta for a true Mediterranean feast.</li>



<li><strong>Bread: </strong>Serve it with a side of crusty bread (such as my <a href="https://foolproofliving.com/olive-bread-recipe/">Olive Bread</a>) or warm <a href="https://foolproofliving.com/homemade-pita-bread-recipe/">pita bread</a> to scoop up every last bit of that delicious dressing.</li>



<li><strong>Fresh fruit: </strong>If all you need is a<strong> </strong>light and refreshing complement, serve it alongside a bowl of seasonal fresh fruit, such as watermelon, berries, or grapes.</li>
</ul>


